{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775329574-VkPqD1LbPtWVgCKsPomp","role":"assistant","created":1775329591,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the annual average CPI-U values:\n- 1992: 140.3167\n- 1993: 144.4583\n- 1994: 148.2250\n\nNow let me extract the interest-bearing debt outstanding for series E and EE for calendar years 1992, 1993, and 1994 from the Treasury Bulletin data.\n\nFrom the Treasury Bulletin 1995_06_page_63.txt (which is more recent and has the 1994 data):\n- Calendar year 1992: 144,724 (interest-bearing debt for Series E and EE)\n- Calendar year 1993: 158,633 (interest-bearing debt for Series E and EE)\n- Calendar year 1994: 166,731 (interest-bearing debt for Series E and EE)\n\nThese values are in millions of nominal dollars.\n\nNow I need to adjust these to constant 1994 dollars using the formula:\nAdjusted value = Nominal value × (CPI_1994 / CPI_year)\n\nLet me calculate:\n- 1992 adjusted: 144,724 × (148.2250 / 140.3167)\n- 1993 adjusted: 158,633 × (148.2250 / 144.4583)\n- 1994 adjusted: 166,731 × (148.2250 / 148.2250) = 166,731\n\nThen calculate the sample z-score of the 1994 value relative to the set of three adjusted values.\nThe sample z-score uses n-1 in the denominator for standard deviation.\n\nLet me calculate this in Python.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_760af36e23464c3c","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 - << 'EOF'\nimport math\n\n# Interest-bearing debt outstanding for Series E and EE (calendar years)\n# From Treasury Bulletin 1995_06_page_63.txt\nnominal_1992 = 144724  # millions\nnominal_1993 = 158633  # millions\nnominal_1994 = 166731  # millions\n\n# Annual average CPI-U values\ncpi_1992 = 140.3167\ncpi_1993 = 144.4583\ncpi_1994 = 148.2250\n\n# Adjust to constant 1994 dollars\nadjusted_1992 = nominal_1992 * (cpi_1994 / cpi_1992)\nadjusted_1993 = nominal_1993 * (cpi_1994 / cpi_1993)\nadjusted_1994 = nominal_1994 * (cpi_1994 / cpi_1994)\n\nprint(f\"Adjusted 1992 (constant 1994$): {adjusted_1992:.2f} millions\")\nprint(f\"Adjusted 1993 (constant 1994$): {adjusted_1993:.2f} millions\")\nprint(f\"Adjusted 1994 (constant 1994$): {adjusted_1994:.2f} millions\")\n\n# Calculate sample mean\nvalues = [adjusted_1992, adjusted_1993, adjusted_1994]\nmean = sum(values) / len(values)\nprint(f\"\\nMean: {mean:.2f}\")\n\n# Calculate sample standard deviation using n-1\n# First compute variance\nvariance = sum((x - mean) ** 2 for x in values) / (len(values) - 1)\nstd_dev = math.sqrt(variance)\nprint(f\"Sample Std Dev (n-1): {std_dev:.2f}\")\n\n# Calculate sample z-score for 1994\nz_score = (adjusted_1994 - mean) / std_dev\nprint(f\"\\nSample z-score of 1994: {z_score:.2f}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
